    "recommendations": "Confirming clear and unobstructed travel along the driveway and access road could improve response times and apparatus movement, particularly given the extended travel distance from the street to the main building. Because the property has a single access point, ensuring that the driveway remains wide enough to support simultaneous ingress and egress of emergency vehicles would support more effective operations. Providing visible address marking at the street frontage may assist responders in locating the property quickly. Coordinating with local fire or emergency services to familiarize responding units with the layout, including the detached structure and limited rear access, could further enhance operational readiness during an incident."
