    "recommendations": "Reducing the density of heavy brush and managing scattered shrubs within the immediate structure perimeter could improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity between the surrounding brushland and the residence. Where vegetation grows in close proximity to the structure, increasing separation between plant material and exterior surfaces may reduce structure exposure and support suppression operations. Managing vegetation within the tree cluster areas to reduce ladder fuel opportunities, and thinning connections between scattered trees and adjacent brush, could further reduce fuel continuity across the property. The long driveway should be maintained to support firefighter access and evacuation, with vegetation along its edges kept trimmed to preserve clearance and visibility. Existing open terrain areas represent a natural fuel break that should be preserved and maintained. Ongoing vegetation management within the mixed cover zones near improvements would support long-term wildfire resilience and property preparedness at this wildland interface location."
